// COVERS MemSqlLexerGrammar: MemSql, host, port, databaseName, useSsl
// COVERS MemSqlFunctionLexerGrammar: MemSqlFunction, functionName, function, ownership, Deployment, identifier, description, activationConfiguration, MemSqlFunctionDeploymentConfiguration, activationConnection, stage
//
// Two unrelated grammars sharing a vendor. MemSqlLexerGrammar is the relational datasource
// spec (###Connection, `specification: MemSql` -- note the spelling differs from the
// connection's own `type: MemSQL`); MemSqlFunctionLexerGrammar is the function activator,
// whose section is `###MemSql` (MemSqlFunctionGrammarParserExtension.java:37).
//
// Activator syntax from TestMemSqlFunctionRoundtrip. There is NO upstream grammar test for
// the MemSql datasource spec at all -- the field list and their types come from the .g4 plus
// MemSqlGrammarParserExtension.visitMemSqlDatasourceSpecification. Two traps that file
// documents and no test does: `port` is a STRING in the grammar and then run through
// Integer.valueOf AT PARSE TIME (line 53), so `port: 'abc';` is a parse failure, not a
// compile failure; `useSsl` is likewise a STRING parsed as a Boolean, not a BOOLEAN literal.
// host and port are required, databaseName and useSsl optional.
//
// `stage` is reachable only as an identifier -- MemSqlFunctionParserGrammar.g4:68 defines the
// rule and nothing references it (`definition` at line 29 admits only memSqlFunction and
// deploymentConfig; deploymentConfig at line 59 holds only activationConnection). The token
// lives on in the `identifier` alternation (line 19), so an element is named with it.
//
// Unlike BigQueryFunction, MemSqlFunction REQUIRES ownership (validateAndExtractRequiredField,
// MemSqlFunctionTreeWalker.java), so even the keyword-named element carries it.
###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection fixture::ms::Conn
{
   store: fixture::ms::Db;
   type: MemSQL;
   specification: MemSql
   {
      host: 'localhost';
      port: '3306';
      databaseName: 'mydb';
      useSsl: 'true';
   };
   auth: UserNamePassword
   {
      baseVaultReference: 'vault/prefix/';
      userNameVaultReference: 'user';
      passwordVaultReference: 'pwd';
   };
}

###MemSql
MemSqlFunction <<fixture::ms::A.test>> {fixture::ms::A.val = 'ok'} fixture::ms::MyFunction
{
   functionName : 'demoFunction';
   function : zxx(Integer[1]):String[1];
   ownership : Deployment { identifier: 'testDeployment' };
   description : 'Its a single store function!';
   activationConfiguration : fixture::ms::Conn;
}

MemSqlFunction fixture::ms::stage
{
   functionName : 'keywordNamedFunction';
   function : zxx(Integer[1]):String[1];
   ownership : Deployment { identifier: 'testDeployment' };
}

MemSqlFunctionDeploymentConfiguration fixture::ms::Config
{
   activationConnection : fixture::ms::Conn;
}
